{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 45, :comments ["<b>For I am YHWH who brings you up.</b> On condition that you accept My commandments I brought you up. Another interpretation: ״For I am YHWH who brings you up״ — in all of them it is written ״I brought out,״ and here it is written ״who brings up.״ Tanna of the school of Rabbi Yishmael: Were it not that I brought Israel up from Egypt only for this — that they not defile themselves with creeping things like the other nations — it would suffice; and it is a distinction for them. This is the sense of מַעֲלָה."], :book :leviticus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 11, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:06:04.966154886Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}